  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        43,
        -105.15617314001807
      ],
      "size": [
        1310.546875,
        298.765625
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Exercise: uncalibrated stereo rectification + disparity\n\nTwo views of the SAME static scene from horizontally-offset camera positions (the scene must have DEPTH - a single plane is degenerate for the fundamental matrix).\n1. ORB features are detected in both views and matched (brute force + Lowe ratio test).\n2. 'Find Fundamental Matrix' estimates F with RANSAC (failure-tolerant: too few matches / degenerate -> found=false).\n3. 'Filter Points By Mask' keeps the RANSAC inliers of each view (same mask, applied in lockstep, so the pairs stay aligned).\n4. 'Stereo Rectify (Uncalibrated)' turns F + the inliers into the two rectifying homographies H1/H2 - no camera intrinsics needed.\n5. Each view is warped by its homography ('CV Array Size' supplies the output size; borderMode=BORDER_CONSTANT so empty areas stay black, not mirrored). After rectification a scene point lands on the SAME row in both views.\n6. 'Stereo Disparity (SGBM)' matches along horizontal scanlines; the heatmap shows disparity (brighter = larger shift = closer). IMPORTANT: uncalibrated rectification fixes H1/H2 only up to an affine ambiguity and least-squares-CENTERS the disparity around zero, so 'min_disparity' must be NEGATIVE (here -48 with num_disparities=96: the search window straddles 0). With min_disparity=0 half the scene falls outside the window and the map degenerates; an over-wide window invites wrong matches on repetitive texture.\n7. The two if/else nodes gate the warps on 'found': an unrectifiable pair passes through unchanged.\n\nDebug: the inlier matches side by side, and H1 ('Inspect CV Data'). Check the rectified previews - corresponding features should sit on the same horizontal line. Tip: switch the detectors to SIFT for wide baselines; widen the (min_disparity, num_disparities) window for nearer objects."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
